@@ -0,0 +1,280 @@
+# PayPal integration plan — Fogline shop
+
+Task: add PayPal checkout (PayPal / Venmo / Pay Later buttons + Pay Later messaging) next to the
+existing card form; fulfil a shop order only after PayPal has really captured the right amount.
+Skills in order: (1) this plan-first APIMatic workflow, (2) `heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6`,
+(3) `heistproof:checkout-hardening` (rule numbers below refer to that skill's table).
+
+## Repo survey (pattern + exemplar)
+
+| Convention | Pattern | Exemplar |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Module format | ESM (`"type": "module"`), Node >=22 (runs 24.x); SDK `instanceof` is reliable within this single dialect | `package.json`, `server.js:1` |
+| Server layering | Express app factory with injected deps `createApp({ db, cards, adminKey })`; routes in `server.js`; domain logic in `lib/*.js`; new PayPal code follows the same split: service in `lib/paypal.js`, routes thin in `server.js` | `server.js:12`, `lib/card-processor.js:5` (factory returning an object of async methods) |
+| Pricing | Server prices the bag from catalog SKUs/qtys; integer cents; browser never sends prices | `lib/cart.js:6` |
+| Persistence | `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync`, synchronous prepared statements; order statuses `pending/paid/failed/fulfilled` | `lib/db.js:6` |
+| Fulfilment | `fulfilOrder(db, orderId)` prints a label per call — must run exactly once per order | `lib/fulfilment.js:3` |
+| Tests | `node:test` + `assert/strict`, real HTTP against `app.listen(0)` | `test/checkout.test.js:8` |
+| Commands | test: `npm test`; start: `npm start`; no build, no linter, no tsconfig (`tsc --noEmit` over touched files is not applicable to this plain-JS project — plain JS with JSDoc-free style; SDK contract compliance is asserted at runtime by the faked-fetch tests, which exercise the SDK's own schema encode/decode. State this in the final report.) | `package.json:9-12` |
+| Baseline (untouched tree) | `npm test` = 5 pass, 0 fail (2026-11-08) | — |
+
+## Toolchain / install
+
+- `paypal` is NOT on npm. Installed from source, pinned to a commit over https (task requirement):
+  `npm install --save-exact "paypal@git+https://github.com/context-plugins/paypal-typescript-sdk#5d0df8a8817e5fdf2e2cd48e68f790ea4730aab2"`
+  → `paypal@2.29.0` (API spec 2.29), Node floor >=20.3 (satisfied), runtime dep `zod ^4.1.0`.
+  `node -e "console.log(require.resolve('paypal/package.json'))"` resolves and
+  `node_modules/paypal/sdk-map.md` + `map/operations/` are present; `import('paypal')` loads.
+  Import specifier is the package root only (`paypal`); no deep imports. The SDK exports a model
+  type named `Error` — if ever imported, alias it (`Error as SdkError`); this JS project imports
+  values only: `PaypalClient`, `PaypalError` (family), `CheckoutPaymentIntent`.
+- Credentials smoke: SKIPPED by task instruction — no PayPal credentials exist while building and
+  no live PayPal calls may be made. The harness runs against the sandbox afterwards.
+- Host decision (contract-sheet item 1): this SDK declares exactly one environment and emits no
+  `ServerEnvironment`; the only host knob is `serverOptions: { baseUrl }` (`src/client-options.ts`
+  shows this SDK's `serverOptions` is the flat `{ baseUrl?: string }`). The shop sets it from
+  `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`). Per the task contract we do NOT
+  fail startup on a (host, credential) pairing: `PAYPAL_API_BASE` is intentionally pointed at a
+  local recording proxy by the harness, and `PAYPAL_ENV` — never the base URL — selects the browser
+  script (`sandbox` → `https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`, `live` →
+  `https://www.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`).
+
+## Configuration contract (env → code)
+
+| Env | Used for | Missing/invalid behaviour |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID` | SDK `oauth2.clientId`; also the only credential sent to the browser | PayPal routes answer 503; config endpoint omits buttons support (see below) |
+| `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET` | SDK `oauth2.clientSecret`; server only, never served | same as above |
+| `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` | `webhook_id` in verify-webhook-signature | webhook endpoint answers 503, changes nothing |
+| `PAYPAL_API_BASE` | `serverOptions.baseUrl` for the SDK (its OAuth token follows the same base) AND the base for the verify-webhook-signature call. Default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com` | default applies |
+| `PAYPAL_ENV` | browser script URL only: `sandbox` (default when unset) or `live` | unknown value → treat as sandbox for the script? NO — fail config: `live` only when exactly `"live"`, else sandbox script. The API host is never derived from it. |
+| `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY` | sandbox only: browser `testBuyerCountry`; unset ⇒ the key is not sent at all | not sent |
+
+Client construction: ONE long-lived `PaypalClient` built in `lib/paypal.js` factory
+(`createPayPalService`), held for the process lifetime (token cache + memoized resources live on
+it; there is no `close()`). Options: `oauth2: { clientId, clientSecret }`,
+`serverOptions: { baseUrl: apiBase }`, `logging: { level: "off" }` (explicit so
+`PAYPAL_CLIENT_LOG` cannot switch logging on; `logRequestBody` stays off — order bodies carry
+amounts/emails we do not log; no per-call `logging` is ever passed), `retry` left at SDK defaults
+except nothing: default gate retries GET/HEAD/PUT/OPTIONS only, so the POST writes are sent exactly
+once by the SDK; the per-attempt `timeout` default 60_000 ms stands. `fetch` is injectable
+(`ClientOptions.fetch`) — the test seam; production uses the global fetch resolved at construction.
+No pagination/streaming exists on this SDK; none is needed. No `fetch` wrapper/middleware is built
+(deliberate omission — nothing in scope needs extra headers; the verify call is outside the SDK, see
+Assumptions).
+
+## Operations in scope (from `map/operations/orders.md`, one pass)
+
+All on `client.orders`, all `Auth: oauth2`, flat channel-blind request objects,
+`ApiPromise<T, E>` throw-based (we `await`; we do not use `.asApiResult()` — no in-scope operation
+resolves to `undefined`, and no success status/headers are needed). None of the 11 `undefined`
+operations is in scope. Error bodies: SDK model `Error` (`src/models/error.ts`):
+`{ name: string, message: string, debugId: string, details?: ErrorDetails[], links? }`,
+`ErrorDetails.issue: string` (`src/models/error-details.ts`). Arm tags are schema-derived
+(per the map they are literally `"error"`, `"error2"`, …); we NEVER switch on `err.payload.kind`
+across operations: we read `err.status` and, for capture, `err.payload.body.details[].issue` /
+`.message` from that operation's own arm table).
+
+### createOrder — `POST /v2/checkout/orders`
+- Signature: `createOrder(request: Orders.CreateOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CreateOrderError>` (request type IS `<Op>Request` here).
+- Fields: `body: OrderRequest` (body, required); headers all optional: `payPalRequestId` (`PayPal-Request-Id`), `prefer` (default `"return=minimal"`), `payPalMockResponse`, `payPalPartnerAttributionId`, `payPalClientMetadataId`, `payPalAuthAssertion`. SDK also mints an `Idempotency-Key` per call (not settable).
+- Returns `Order` (`src/models/order.ts`, ALL members optional — assert `id !== undefined` after the call; a missing id is an unknown outcome, not a success).
+- Error arms: `"error"`[400] · `"error2"`[401] · `"error3"`[422] · `"error4"`[default] · `"undeclared"`[rawBody], all body `Error` except undeclared.
+
+### captureOrder — `POST /v2/checkout/orders/{id}/capture`
+- Signature: `captureOrder(request: Orders.CaptureOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CaptureOrderError>`.
+- Fields: `id` (path, required); `body?: OrderCaptureRequest` (optional — omit); headers optional incl. `payPalRequestId`, `prefer` (default `"return=minimal"`).
+- Returns `Order`. Settlement data read from it: `purchaseUnits[].payments.captures[]`
+  (`OrdersCapture`, `src/models/orders-capture.ts`: `status?: CaptureStatus`, `id?`, `amount?: Money{currencyCode,value}`, `customId?`),
+  `purchaseUnits[].customId` (`PurchaseUnit`, `src/models/purchase-unit.ts`), `status?: OrderStatus`.
+  Every member is optional ⇒ assert each one we depend on; absence = unknown, never paid.
+- Error arms: `"error"`[400] · `"error2"`[401] · `"error3"`[403] · `"error4"`[404] · `"error5"`[422] · `"error6"`[500] · `"error7"`[default] · `"undeclared"`.
+
+### getOrder — `GET /v2/checkout/orders/{id}`
+- Signature: `getOrder(request: Orders.GetOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.GetOrderError>`.
+- Fields: `id` (path, required); `fields` (query, optional — omit); mock/auth-assertion headers (omit).
+- Returns `Order` (same assertions as capture). Error arms: `"error"`[401] · `"error2"`[404] · `"error3"`[default] · `"undeclared"`.
+
+### Models set on create (required vs optional)
+- `OrderRequest` (`src/models/order-request.ts`): `intent: CheckoutPaymentIntent` REQUIRED
+  (= `CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture` = `"CAPTURE"`, `src/models/checkout-payment-intent.ts`),
+  `purchaseUnits: PurchaseUnitRequest[]` REQUIRED; `processingInstruction?`, `payer?`,
+  `paymentSource?`, `applicationContext?` optional.
+- `PurchaseUnitRequest` (`src/models/purchase-unit-request.ts`): `amount: AmountWithBreakdown`
+  REQUIRED; `referenceId?`, `payee?`, `paymentInstruction?`, `description?`, `customId?`,
+  `invoiceId?`, `softDescriptor?`, `items?`, `shipping?`, `supplementaryData?` optional.
+- `AmountWithBreakdown` (`src/models/amount-with-breakdown.ts`): `currencyCode: string`,
+  `value: string` REQUIRED (money stays a string end-to-end), `breakdown?` optional;
+  `AmountBreakdown.itemTotal?: Money` (`src/models/amount-breakdown.ts`).
+- `ItemRequest` (`src/models/item-request.ts`): `name: string`, `unitAmount: Money`,
+  `quantity: string` REQUIRED; `sku?` optional. `Money` = `{ currencyCode, value }` both required
+  (`src/models/money.ts`).
+- Enums are open: `CaptureStatus.Completed === "COMPLETED"` etc. (`src/models/capture-status.ts`);
+  compare against the const members, keep a default arm for unknown values.
+- Money conversion (hardening rule 2): integer cents → decimal string in ONE function
+  `centsToPayPalAmount` in `lib/paypal.js` (4900 → `"49.00"`, 5 → `"0.05"`), with a unit test.
+  Currency: catalog/cart currency is `usd` → sent as `"USD"`. Item breakdown: `item_total` equals
+  the total (no tax/shipping in this shop), items carry per-unit amounts whose
+  `unit × qty` sums to the total.
+
+## Webhook verification — NOT an SDK operation (verified)
+The SDK map contains no webhook/verify operation (searched `map/` and `src/`: no
+`verify-webhook-signature`, no notifications resource; client-initialization skill confirms
+generated SDKs have no webhook surface). Per hardening rule 6 this one call is therefore a direct
+REST call, still bound by the task contract to the same base:
+`POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` with a client-credentials
+access token obtained from `POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/oauth2/token` (Basic client id:secret,
+`grant_type=client_credentials`; token cached in the service until shortly before expiry).
+Body: `{ auth_algo, cert_url, transmission_id, transmission_sig, transmission_time }` copied from
+the `PAYPAL-*` request headers, plus `webhook_id: PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` and
+`webhook_event: <parsed JSON body>`. Act only on `verification_status === "SUCCESS"`; anything
+else (including a failed/unreachable verification) → HTTP 400, no state change.
+
+## HTTP surface this shop exposes
+
+| Route | Behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /api/paypal/config` | `{ clientId, scriptUrl, currency: "USD", ...(sandbox && PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY ? { testBuyerCountry } : {}) }`. Never the secret (rule 12). |
+| `POST /api/paypal/orders` | Body `{ items, email? }` only — price/amount/total/currency fields ignored (rule 1). Prices via `priceCart` (rule 11 validation reused). Creates the shop order FIRST (pending, method `paypal`), then SDK createOrder with `custom_id`/`invoice_id` = shop order id (rule 3), stores the PayPal order id on the shop order (UNIQUE). Returns `{ id: <paypalOrderId>, orderId: <shopOrderId> }`. |
+| `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` | Looks the shop order up by PayPal order id (404 if unknown). Already paid/fulfilled → 200 with current status (no second capture). Else SDK captureOrder, then settle (below). Declined-instrument → 402-ish JSON telling the buyer to choose another way to pay, order stays pending. |
+| `POST /api/paypal/webhooks` | Verify (above) → 400 on failure. Then claim the event id (unique), then act: only `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` can settle an order, and only by re-reading the order via SDK getOrder and applying the same settlement checks. `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` and everything else: recorded, 200, no state change (rules 4, 9). |
+| `GET /api/orders/:id` (existing) | unchanged; browser polls it for the final status. |
+
+Settlement (shared by capture response and webhook path) — mark paid ONLY if ALL hold (rule 4):
+order id matches; a capture exists with `status === "COMPLETED"`; capture amount parsed exactly
+(decimal string → cents, no floats) equals the shop order total; capture currency equals the shop
+currency (case-insensitive); the purchase unit's (or capture's) `custom_id` equals the shop order
+id. `PENDING` capture → leave pending, answer 202 `pending` (rule 5); the
+`PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook settles it later.
+
+Browser (`public/index.html`, `public/app.js`, web-sdk-v6 skill): server-templated? No — the page
+fetches `/api/paypal/config`, injects the script URL from config (never hard-codes env), then
+`paypal.createInstance({ clientId, components: ["paypal-payments","venmo-payments","paypal-messages"], pageType: "checkout", ...(testBuyerCountry ? { testBuyerCountry } : {}) })`,
+`findEligibleMethods({ currencyCode: "USD" })`, renders `<paypal-button>`, `<venmo-button>`,
+`<paypal-pay-later-button>` (hidden until eligible; Pay Later gets `productCode`/`countryCode` from
+`getDetails("paylater")`), one session per method via
+`createPayPalOneTimePaymentSession` / `createVenmoOneTimePaymentSession` /
+`createPayLaterOneTimePaymentSession`; on click: start `createOrder()` WITHOUT awaiting before
+`session.start({ presentationMode: "auto" }, createOrderPromise)` (transient activation);
+`onApprove` POSTs the capture route and only the server's answer decides; Pay Later
+`<paypal-message amount currency-code="USD" auto-bootstrap>` created via
+`sdk.createPayPalMessages()`, amount updated on `bag:change`. Card form untouched.
+
+### 1b.1 — DURABLE WRITES
+
+DUPLICATE CLAIMS
+
+| Write | Where the claim is stored | What rejects the second one | Where that rejection is caught | Where in the code |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| create PayPal order | shop `orders` row (status `pending`, method `paypal`) created BEFORE the SDK call; its id is the `custom_id`/`invoice_id` and the `PayPal-Request-Id` header value | the row's existence + `paypal_order_id` UNIQUE column: storing a second PayPal order id for the same shop order, or the same PayPal id on two shop orders, is refused by SQLite (`SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE` — check the driver error code/message, not a pre-read) | the binding in the create route (`server.js` `db.setPayPalOrderId` call); on constraint failure the already-bound record is used | `server.js` create route + `lib/db.js` `setPayPalOrderId` (UNIQUE index) |
+| capture / mark paid + fulfil | the shop `orders` row itself: conditional `UPDATE orders SET status='paid', … WHERE id=? AND status='pending'` | the conditional UPDATE changes 0 rows for the second caller (SQLite serialises the write) | not an exception: `db.claimPaid` returns whether its conditional UPDATE changed 1 row; only the winner calls `fulfilOrder`; the loser reads and returns the current status | `lib/db.js` `claimPaid`, called from `server.js` `settleFromPayPalOrder` |
+| record webhook event | `paypal_events.event_id` PRIMARY KEY inserted BEFORE acting | the PK insert is refused (`SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_PRIMARYKEY`/UNIQUE) on redelivery | the changes-check on the insert in the webhook route; a duplicate answers 200 and changes nothing | `lib/db.js` `recordEvent` (`INSERT OR IGNORE` on the PK), called from `server.js` webhook route |
+
+Claim release: a create whose SDK call is refused with an API error (never reached PayPal)
+marks the shop order `failed`, freeing the buyer to start a fresh checkout; a capture claim is
+the status transition itself and is never released backwards (rule 9). The SDK-minted
+`Idempotency-Key` goes beside these claims, never in place of them; our deterministic
+`PayPal-Request-Id` (= shop order id on create, `capture-<shopOrderId>` on capture) is the
+caller-supplied key that spans our own retries of the same logical write.
+
+UNKNOWN OUTCOMES
+
+| Write | The operation you re-read with | The reference you search by | Where in the code | The test that fails the connection |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| captureOrder | `getOrder` | the PayPal order id (path `id`) we captured | `server.js` capture route (on `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` or unknown outcome, re-reads via `lib/paypal.js` `getOrder`, then `settleFromPayPalOrder`) | `test/paypal.test.js`: "a dropped connection on capture re-reads the order" (asserts the GET was made) and "ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED settles by re-reading the order" |
+| createOrder | none exists — PayPal offers no lookup by `PayPal-Request-Id`/`custom_id` (see Blockers); a never-sent failure (`auth`/`encode`) is reported as failed and the shop order marked `failed`; a connection/timeout/decode-on-2xx is reported UNKNOWN (502, shop order left `pending`, never fulfilled) | n/a | `server.js` create route + `lib/paypal.js` `createOrder`/`translatePayPalError` | `test/paypal.test.js`: "a dropped connection on capture re-reads the order; on create it does not" (auth-failure half asserts no orders call followed a never-sent failure) |
+
+### 1b.2 — CROSS-OPERATION INVARIANTS
+
+| Invariant | Where the legal set comes from | Enforced where | The test that proves it |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A PayPal order id presented to the capture route must be one this shop created | this application's `orders.paypal_order_id` column (read by exact lookup) | capture route, BEFORE the capture claim/SDK call | capture for an unknown PayPal id → 404 and the fake fetch sees NO capture request |
+| The capture that settles an order must carry `custom_id` = that shop order and amount/currency = its server-priced total | the bound shop order row | settlement function shared by capture + webhook | fake capture with wrong amount or wrong `custom_id` → unpaid, unshipped, no fulfil |
+| SKUs/quantities in a create request must be catalog SKUs with integer qty 1–10 | `lib/catalog.js` via `priceCart` | create route before any SDK call | bad bag → 400 and no PayPal request is made |
+
+### 1b.3 — OPTIONAL REQUEST FIELDS
+
+createOrder (`Orders.CreateOrderRequest` + body):
+
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `payPalRequestId` | DUPLICATE CLAIMS row (create): the reference spanning our retries | ✅ `= shopOrderId` |
+| `prefer` | settlement needs the full representation (purchase units, custom_id) asserted, not the minimal default | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| `payPalMockResponse` | nothing (harness injects it on ITS calls if wanted; we never set it) | ❌ leave it out |
+| `payPalPartnerAttributionId` | nothing | ❌ |
+| `payPalClientMetadataId` | nothing | ❌ |
+| `payPalAuthAssertion` | nothing | ❌ |
+| `body.intent` | the task: CAPTURE intent checkout | ✅ `CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture` |
+| `body.purchaseUnits` | the task: the priced bag | ✅ one unit (below) |
+| `body.processingInstruction` / `payer` / `paymentSource` / `applicationContext` | nothing | ❌ |
+| `purchaseUnits[].amount` | the task (server-priced total) | ✅ `{ currencyCode: "USD", value: centsToPayPalAmount(total), breakdown: { itemTotal: same } }` (rule 2) |
+| `purchaseUnits[].customId` | hardening rule 3 + CROSS-OPERATION row | ✅ `= shopOrderId` |
+| `purchaseUnits[].invoiceId` | hardening rule 3 ("if you like") — chosen for reconciliation | ✅ `= shopOrderId` |
+| `purchaseUnits[].items` | rule 2: breakdown whose sum equals the total | ✅ `{ name, sku, quantity: String(qty), unitAmount }` per line |
+| `purchaseUnits[].referenceId` / `payee` / `paymentInstruction` / `description` / `softDescriptor` / `shipping` / `supplementaryData` | nothing | ❌ |
+| item `tax` / `description` / `url` / `category` / `imageUrl` / `upc` / `billingPlan` | nothing | ❌ |
+
+captureOrder: `id` ✅ (path, the PayPal order id); `prefer` ✅ `"return=representation"`
+(settlement reads captures from the response); `payPalRequestId` ✅ `= "capture-" + shopOrderId`
+(DUPLICATE CLAIMS/UNKNOWN rows); `body` ❌ (nothing requires an `OrderCaptureRequest`);
+`payPalMockResponse`/`payPalClientMetadataId`/`payPalAuthAssertion` ❌.
+getOrder: `id` ✅; `fields` ❌; mock/auth-assertion headers ❌.
+
+Proof test: the faked-fetch tests assert the exact JSON body + headers the SDK sent for create and
+capture — no key beyond the ✅ rows (SDK-added auth/content-type/idempotency-key are the SDK's, not
+ours).
+
+### 1b.4 — WHEN THE API SAYS NO
+
+createOrder (data = bag the caller typed):
+
+| status | your app answers | the caller reads | test |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| a `4xx` other than 401/403/429 | the same `4xx` | the API's reason text from `err.payload` (`body.message` + detail issues) | fake a 422 with a reason; assert the reason is in the response |
+| 401 / 403 | 502 | fixed: "PayPal is unavailable." (our credentials) | fake a 401; assert 502 + fixed message |
+| 429 | 503 | fixed: "PayPal is busy; try again shortly." (our quota) | — |
+| 5xx | 502 | fixed: "PayPal is unavailable." | — |
+| no response (connection/timeout/decode-on-2xx) | 502 | fixed UNKNOWN message — never "failed"; shop order left pending | connection-failure test asserts 502-unknown and no fulfil |
+| no response, never sent (`auth`/`encode`) | 502 | fixed message; shop order marked failed (nothing reached PayPal) | auth-failure test asserts no re-read is attempted |
+
+captureOrder (data = the PayPal order id the caller supplies):
+
+| status | your app answers | the caller reads | test |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `422` with `details[].issue === "INSTRUMENT_DECLINED"` | 402 | fixed buyer-facing: choose another way to pay (rule 5); order stays pending | fake the 422; assert 402 + pending + no shipment |
+| a `4xx` other than 401/403/429 (incl. `TRANSACTION_REFUSED`, `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` is handled by re-read, not this row) | the same `4xx` | the API's reason text from `err.payload` | fake a 422 with a reason; assert it is in the response |
+| 401 / 403 | 502 | fixed: "PayPal is unavailable." | fake a 401; assert 502 + fixed message |
+| 429 | 503 | fixed quota message | — |
+| 5xx | 502 | fixed message | — |
+| no response, on this write | per UNKNOWN OUTCOMES: `getOrder` re-read, settle from what PayPal holds; still unknown if that fails | unknown — never "failed" | connection-failure test asserts the getOrder request WAS made; `auth`/`encode` test asserts it was NOT |
+
+getOrder (read): 4xx-other → same status + reason; 401/403 → 502 fixed; 429 → 503 fixed;
+5xx → 502 fixed; no response on a read → 502 fixed.
+Logging: on every `api` error we log `err.status`, the payload's `message`/`debugId`
+(correlation id) — and still return the reason per the tables; SDK `err.message` (method+URL)
+never goes on the wire.
+
+## Assumptions & Blockers
+
+- Minor: currency is USD throughout (catalog/cart are USD-only); amounts are decimal strings.
+- Minor: email is optional in the PayPal flow (existing card flow already tolerates a missing one).
+- BLOCKER-noted, resolved by design (not awaiting the user — the task contract fixes the answer):
+  the SDK has no operation to find a created order by our reference and no webhook-verify
+  operation. Create-order unknown outcomes are therefore reported UNKNOWN with the shop order left
+  `pending` (never fulfilled), and webhook verification uses the direct REST call in the contract
+  above against `PAYPAL_API_BASE`. No other PayPal call bypasses the SDK.
+- Minor: the shop DB may already exist; new columns/tables are added idempotently at open.
+
+## REQUIRED READING
+
+| Step | Skill |
+| --- | --- |
+| Client construction & lifetime | MUST load `paypal:typescript-client-initialization` ✅ loaded |
+| Credentials / OAuth token lifecycle | MUST load `paypal:typescript-authentication` ✅ loaded |
+| Calling operations, `.asApiResult()` discipline | MUST load `paypal:typescript-calling-endpoints` ✅ loaded |
+| Model shapes, open enums, optional-vs-nullable | MUST load `paypal:typescript-models` ✅ loaded |
+| Error boundary (always) | MUST load `paypal:typescript-error-handling` ✅ loaded |
+| Base-URL override, retry/logging posture | MUST load `paypal:typescript-configuration-resilience` ✅ loaded |
+| Faked-fetch tests (before the first test file) | MUST load `paypal:typescript-testing` ✅ loaded |
+| Browser buttons + messaging | MUST load `heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6` ✅ loaded |
+| Attack rules 1–12 | MUST load `heistproof:checkout-hardening` ✅ loaded |
